												</table>
																					</div>
																		</section>

																		<!-- ====================================================
																		     generated table labels. The prose table above
																		     is HAND-WRITTEN: every cell carries its own
																		     data-label, because a person typed it. The
																		     consumer that motivated the component
																		     (hermes-articles) cannot do that - it renders
																		     397 markdown pipe-tables from a converter
																		     that emits <th scope="col"> and nothing
																		     else - so on a phone every one of those
																		     tables stacked into unlabelled values, and
																		     the stacked layout's whole point was gone.

																		     `data-cm-table-labels` derives them from the
																		     header row at runtime. The specimen below is
																		     deliberately UNLABELLED in the markup, so it
																		     proves the derivation rather than restating
																		     it: shrink the window to see the labels
																		     appear at the same moment the rows stack. -->
																		<section id="tablelabels" class="cm-section cm-section--pad" data-cm-table-labels>
																			<SectionHead title="generated table labels">
												<code>[data-cm-table-labels]</code> copies each header's text onto the body cells as <code>data-label</code>, which is what <code>.cm-prose-table</code> reads with <code>content: attr(data-label)</code> once it stacks. Below 760px this table has <strong>no</strong> <code>data-label</code> anywhere in its markup, and the labels on the right of each value are derived. An author's own <code>data-label</code> is never overwritten, and the attribute is opt-in because rewriting cells behind someone's back is not something to do to a table a person wrote.
																			</SectionHead>

																			<div class="cm-prose">
																				<p>A generated table keeps its column names on a phone:</p>
																				<table class="cm-prose-table">
																					<caption>Costs per million tokens, published 2026-10-03.</caption>
																					<thead>
																						<tr>
																							<th scope="col">Model</th>
