			<section id="scrollarea" class="cm-section cm-section--pad">
				<SectionHead title="scroll area">
A bounded vertical scrollport: the box grows to <code>--scroll-h</code> (14rem
					here) and then scrolls its OWN content, so a long list costs page
					height once instead of forever. <code>overscroll-behavior: contain</code>
					keeps the end of the list from dragging the page behind it - the
					same containment a capped table wrapper gets, as a class you can
					put on any list.
				</SectionHead>
				<div class="cm-scrollarea" style="--scroll-h: 14rem;
						border: 1px solid var(--line); padding: var(--space-2) 0;">
					<ul style="list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0;">
					<li class="cm-row"><span class="cm-row__title">node-01.example.internal</span><span class="cm-row__meta">10.0.1.1</span></li>
					<li class="cm-row"><span class="cm-row__title">node-02.example.internal</span><span class="cm-row__meta">10.0.2.2</span></li>
					<li class="cm-row"><span class="cm-row__title">node-03.example.internal</span><span class="cm-row__meta">10.0.3.3</span></li>
					<li class="cm-row"><span class="cm-row__title">node-04.example.internal</span><span class="cm-row__meta">10.0.4.4</span></li>
					<li class="cm-row"><span class="cm-row__title">node-05.example.internal</span><span class="cm-row__meta">10.0.5.5</span></li>
					<li class="cm-row"><span class="cm-row__title">node-06.example.internal</span><span class="cm-row__meta">10.0.6.6</span></li>
					<li class="cm-row"><span class="cm-row__title">node-07.example.internal</span><span class="cm-row__meta">10.0.7.7</span></li>
					<li class="cm-row"><span class="cm-row__title">node-08.example.internal</span><span class="cm-row__meta">10.0.8.8</span></li>
					<li class="cm-row"><span class="cm-row__title">node-09.example.internal</span><span class="cm-row__meta">10.0.9.9</span></li>
					<li class="cm-row"><span class="cm-row__title">node-10.example.internal</span><span class="cm-row__meta">10.0.10.10</span></li>
					<li class="cm-row"><span class="cm-row__title">node-11.example.internal</span><span class="cm-row__meta">10.0.11.11</span></li>
					<li class="cm-row"><span class="cm-row__title">node-12.example.internal</span><span class="cm-row__meta">10.0.12.12</span></li>
					<li class="cm-row"><span class="cm-row__title">node-13.example.internal</span><span class="cm-row__meta">10.0.13.13</span></li>
					<li class="cm-row"><span class="cm-row__title">node-14.example.internal</span><span class="cm-row__meta">10.0.14.14</span></li>
					</ul>
				</div>
			</section>
			<section id="utilities" class="cm-section cm-section--pad">
				<SectionHead title="utilities">
Two helpers shadcn ships under utils, in house CSS. <code>scroll-fade</code>
					masks a scrollport's own edges off ITS OWN scroll position:
					<code>animation-timeline: scroll(self ...)</code> is the entire
					mechanism - no scroll listeners, nothing on the main thread, and
					every cut edge shows its fade exactly while content is cut there.
					The composition below is deliberate: <code>.cm-scrollarea</code>
					owns the box, <code>.cm-scroll-fade</code> owns the edges.
					<code>shimmer</code> sweeps a highlight derived from
					<code>currentColor</code> across text - readable at every frame,
					off under reduced motion, and absent (not invisible) where
					<code>background-clip: text</code> is unsupported.
				</SectionHead>
				<div class="cm-scrollarea cm-scroll-fade" style="--scroll-h: 12rem; border: 1px solid var(--line); padding: var(--space-2) 0;">
					<ul style="list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0;">
					<li class="cm-row"><span class="cm-row__title">node-01.example.internal</span><span class="cm-row__meta">10.0.1.1</span></li>
					<li class="cm-row"><span class="cm-row__title">node-02.example.internal</span><span class="cm-row__meta">10.0.2.2</span></li>
					<li class="cm-row"><span class="cm-row__title">node-03.example.internal</span><span class="cm-row__meta">10.0.3.3</span></li>
					<li class="cm-row"><span class="cm-row__title">node-04.example.internal</span><span class="cm-row__meta">10.0.4.4</span></li>
					<li class="cm-row"><span class="cm-row__title">node-05.example.internal</span><span class="cm-row__meta">10.0.5.5</span></li>
					<li class="cm-row"><span class="cm-row__title">node-06.example.internal</span><span class="cm-row__meta">10.0.6.6</span></li>
					<li class="cm-row"><span class="cm-row__title">node-07.example.internal</span><span class="cm-row__meta">10.0.7.7</span></li>
					<li class="cm-row"><span class="cm-row__title">node-08.example.internal</span><span class="cm-row__meta">10.0.8.8</span></li>
					<li class="cm-row"><span class="cm-row__title">node-09.example.internal</span><span class="cm-row__meta">10.0.9.9</span></li>
					<li class="cm-row"><span class="cm-row__title">node-10.example.internal</span><span class="cm-row__meta">10.0.10.10</span></li>
					<li class="cm-row"><span class="cm-row__title">node-11.example.internal</span><span class="cm-row__meta">10.0.11.11</span></li>
					<li class="cm-row"><span class="cm-row__title">node-12.example.internal</span><span class="cm-row__meta">10.0.12.12</span></li>
					</ul>
				</div>
				<p class="cm-head__sub">
					The horizontal case is the one tables need: the end of the row
					fades while more of it lies to the right, sharpens when you reach
					the end, and the start fades to say how far you have come.
					<code>.cm-scroll-fade-x</code> sits on every
					<code>.cm-table-wrap</code> for exactly that reason.
				</p>
				<p class="cm-head__sub">
					Every modifier, one box each - the edges it names are the edges
					that fade, the rest stay sharp; the px steps are the size sugar,
					and <code>--none</code> is the stop sign (no mask, no timeline).
					The inline styles are the box chrome only; the class carries the
					behaviour.
				</p>
				<div style="display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: var(--space-2); margin-top: var(--space-2);">
					<div class="cm-scroll-fade-y cm-scroll-fade--t" style="width: 7rem; height: 4rem; overflow-y: auto; border: 1px solid var(--line); padding: var(--space-1); font-size: var(--text-xs);">top edge only<br>line two<br>line three<br>line four<br>line five</div>
					<div class="cm-scroll-fade cm-scroll-fade--b" style="width: 7rem; height: 4rem; overflow-y: auto; border: 1px solid var(--line); padding: var(--space-1); font-size: var(--text-xs);">bottom edge only<br>line two<br>line three<br>line four<br>line five</div>
					<div class="cm-scroll-fade-x cm-scroll-fade--l" style="width: 7rem; height: 2.6rem; overflow-x: auto; border: 1px solid var(--line); padding: var(--space-1); font-size: var(--text-xs);"><span style="white-space: nowrap;">left edge: the long row scrolls on in this direction and fades behind</span></div>
					<div class="cm-scroll-fade-x cm-scroll-fade--r" style="width: 7rem; height: 2.6rem; overflow-x: auto; border: 1px solid var(--line); padding: var(--space-1); font-size: var(--text-xs);"><span style="white-space: nowrap;">right edge: the long row scrolls on in this direction and fades ahead</span></div>
					<div class="cm-scroll-fade-x cm-scroll-fade--s" style="width: 7rem; height: 2.6rem; overflow-x: auto; border: 1px solid var(--line); padding: var(--space-1); font-size: var(--text-xs);"><span style="white-space: nowrap;">logical start: in LTR this is the left edge, the same single-sided fade</span></div>
					<div class="cm-scroll-fade-x cm-scroll-fade--e" style="width: 7rem; height: 2.6rem; overflow-x: auto; border: 1px solid var(--line); padding: var(--space-1); font-size: var(--text-xs);"><span style="white-space: nowrap;">logical end: in LTR this is the right edge, the fade that hints more</span></div>
					<div class="cm-scroll-fade cm-scroll-fade--4" style="width: 7rem; height: 4rem; overflow-y: auto; border: 1px solid var(--line); padding: var(--space-1); font-size: var(--text-xs);">--4: a 4px fade<br>line two<br>line three<br>line four</div>
					<div class="cm-scroll-fade cm-scroll-fade--8" style="width: 7rem; height: 4rem; overflow-y: auto; border: 1px solid var(--line); padding: var(--space-1); font-size: var(--text-xs);">--8: an 8px fade<br>line two<br>line three<br>line four</div>
					<div class="cm-scroll-fade cm-scroll-fade--16" style="width: 7rem; height: 4rem; overflow-y: auto; border: 1px solid var(--line); padding: var(--space-1); font-size: var(--text-xs);">--16: a 16px fade<br>line two<br>line three<br>line four</div>
					<div class="cm-scroll-fade cm-scroll-fade--32" style="width: 7rem; height: 4rem; overflow-y: auto; border: 1px solid var(--line); padding: var(--space-1); font-size: var(--text-xs);">--32: a 32px fade<br>line two<br>line three<br>line four</div>
					<div class="cm-scroll-fade cm-scroll-fade--none" style="width: 7rem; height: 4rem; overflow-y: auto; border: 1px solid var(--line); padding: var(--space-1); font-size: var(--text-xs);">--none: no mask at all<br>line two<br>line three<br>line four</div>
				</div>
				<div class="cm-scroll-fade-x" style="overflow-x: auto; border: 1px solid var(--line); padding: var(--space-2);">
					<span style="white-space: nowrap; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: var(--text-xs);">GET https://cdn.mrx.sh/assets/app.9f2c1a.js -> 200 in 4.2ms (cache hit, edge eu-west) | GET https://cdn.mrx.sh/assets/app.9f2c1a.css -> 200 in 1.1ms | GET https://links.mrx.sh/ -> 200 in 88ms | HEAD plex.mrx.sh/library/sections/ -> 304 in 0.9ms | GET https://cdn.mrx.sh/assets/app.9f2c1a.js -> 200 in 4.2ms (cache hit, edge eu-west)</span>
				</div>
				<p class="cm-head__sub">
					<code class="cm-shimmer">cm-shimmer</code> sweeps;
					<code class="cm-shimmer cm-shimmer--once">--once</code> runs a single pass;
					<code class="cm-shimmer cm-shimmer--reverse">--reverse</code> runs it back;
					<code class="cm-shimmer cm-shimmer--none">--none</code> declines - the same
					plain text reduced motion leaves behind. Durations, spread, angle and
					the highlight itself are knobs: <code>--shimmer-duration</code>,
					<code>--shimmer-spread</code>, <code>--shimmer-angle</code>.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section id="chat" class="cm-section cm-section--pad">
				<SectionHead title="chat">
					three parts of a conversation, composed from house primitives: the
					surface (<code>.cm-bubble</code> - seven tones, sharp corners, sized to
					content up to 80% of the row), the row (<code>.cm-msg</code> - avatar
					anchored to the bottom, header and footer that follow the message
					side), and the system note (<code>.cm-marker</code> - inline, bordered,
					or a labeled separator). Tones are border and ink treatments, never
					hues; the docs pair them with text and alignment for exactly this
					reason.
				</SectionHead>
				<div class="cm-spec">
					<div class="cm-spec__row">
						<span class="cm-spec__label">bubble / variants</span>
						<span class="cm-spec__val">7 tones, 80% cap</span>
					</div>
					<div class="cm-spec__row">
						<span class="cm-spec__label">marker / variants</span>
						<span class="cm-spec__val">inline, border, separator</span>
					</div>
				</div>
				<div class="cm-bubble-group" style="width: 100%;">
					<div class="cm-bubble">default - the strong one, usually "me"</div>
					<div class="cm-bubble cm-bubble--secondary">secondary - the standard neutral bubble</div>
					<div class="cm-bubble cm-bubble--muted">muted - quiet supporting content</div>
					<div class="cm-bubble cm-bubble--tinted">tinted - a soft accent wash</div>
					<div class="cm-bubble cm-bubble--outline">outline - bordered, unframed fill</div>
					<div class="cm-bubble cm-bubble--danger">danger - the build failed during install; see the logs</div>
					<div class="cm-bubble cm-bubble--ghost">ghost - assistant text with no frame, full width,
						<code>code allowed</code></div>
				</div>
				<div class="cm-bubble-group" style="width: 100%; margin-top: var(--space-4);">
					<div class="cm-bubble cm-bubble--secondary">aligned to the start - the default side</div>
					<div class="cm-bubble cm-bubble--end">aligned to the end - the user's side</div>
				</div>
