			<section id="navmenu" class="cm-section cm-section--pad">
				<SectionHead title="navigation menu">
					the nav that opens <em>panels</em>, not lists: a persistent
					trigger per section, a chevron drawn from the label's own ink,
					and a panel of links with a description under each - a table of
					contents, which is what a nav panel is. The panel, its light
					dismiss and its focus return are the dropdown's, so the only
					new machinery is the BAR: while a panel is open, Left/Right
					walk the words and the neighbouring panel opens in the same
					press. The indicator under the bar is measured from the page,
					never authored - the runtime reads the section each link points
					at and moves the mark to the one the reader has reached, and
					sets <code>aria-current</code> on that trigger and no other. A
					trigger with no <code>href</code> opens a panel and is never
					the current section, which is why <code>product</code> below
					carries no mark.
				</SectionHead>
				<div class="cm-spec">
					<div class="cm-spec__row">
						<span class="cm-spec__label">runtime</span>
						<span class="cm-spec__val">init measures; scroll and resize re-measure</span>
					</div>
					<div class="cm-spec__row">
						<span class="cm-spec__label">bar</span>
						<span class="cm-spec__val">left/right while open; the next panel opens in the same press</span>
					</div>
					<div class="cm-spec__row">
						<span class="cm-spec__label">current</span>
						<span class="cm-spec__val">measured from the section, then written as aria-current</span>
					</div>
				</div>
