			<section id="scroller" class="cm-section cm-section--pad">
				<SectionHead title="message scroller">
					the transcript frame: a labelled, keyboard-focusable scroll
					region whose <code>data-scrollable</code> tokens drive the
					controls - a button with nothing to scroll toward goes
					<code>inert</code>, <code>tabindex="-1"</code> and
					<code>data-active="false"</code>, so it is never an extra
					focus stop. Rows are addressable (<code>data-message-id</code>)
					and skip off-screen paint work; the outline jumps by message id,
					highlights the current anchored turn, and marks rows on screen -
					tracking runs only because the outline asks for it. Growing
					content pins the live edge while following; scroll away and the
					pill appears.
				</SectionHead>
				<div class="cm-spec">
					<div class="cm-spec__row">
						<span class="cm-spec__label">runtime</span>
						<span class="cm-spec__val">data-cm-scroller (init + observer)</span>
